  "body": "## What changed\n\nRelease the centre cache when no handle mode can use the selected part.\nKeep the shared cache while Rotate uses it.\nMove glyph drawing into `viewport_bar_glyphs.rs`.\nThe Move glyph now shows a part with three handles.\nPan keeps its four arrows.\nThe bar has 259 lines. The glyph module has 214 lines.\nKeep every existing test and add seven tests.\n\nRecord the remaining decisions in `docs/decisions/2508-move-handle-cleanup.md`.\nDefer the shell split and its separate CRLF conversion until fewer PRs change the shell.\nKeep the crate-wide formatting check unused. Format the new module only.\n\n## Cause\n\n`handles` returned early without clearing the centre cache.\nThe cache kept the last part's facet reference after Move stopped using it.\nMove and Pan both used a four-arm cross.\nGlyph drawing also kept the bar file above the file-size limit.\n\n## Tests\n\nCache release pins:\n\n- `center_cache_releases_facets_when_move_is_off`\n- `center_cache_releases_facets_without_a_selection`\n- `center_cache_releases_facets_when_the_part_is_hidden`\n- `center_cache_releases_facets_when_the_part_is_deleted`\n- `center_cache_releases_facets_when_rotate_has_no_part`\n\nEach release pin fails with the original `move_drag.rs` and passes with the fix.\nThe first four also failed before production code changed.\n`center_cache_keeps_rotate_facets_between_move_handle_passes` passes before and after the change.\nThis test checks that Rotate still reuses the shared cache.\n\n`move_glyph_shows_a_part_body_while_pan_shows_only_arrows` fails before the change and passes with the fix.\nRestoring the original `viewport_bar.rs` makes it fail again.\nRestoring the fix makes it pass again.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes all nine steps.\nThe UI unit suite reports 1161 passed and seven ignored.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\n`git diff --check` passes.\nAll six diff hunks have a written justification outside the branch.\nThe shared sccache wrapper stalled. These checks passed with the wrapper disabled.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff contains no `.nc`, `.cl`, or snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Viewport bar screenshots\n\nBoth images use the application drawing code at three pixels per point.\nThe Move and Pan labels identify the two buttons for review.\nThe images are on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n| Before (`8643d9bb7`) | After (`47626dccdbcf330a192e26ebe5b7ebcbaee2322f`) |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Viewport bar before: Move and Pan](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/1a1b33620794cd34cb7283efa0867a7f98cf09e4/pr-2541/viewport-bar-before.png?raw=true) | ![Viewport bar after: Move and Pan](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/1a1b33620794cd34cb7283efa0867a7f98cf09e4/pr-2541/viewport-bar-after.png?raw=true) |\n\nThe old Move glyph has four arms with balls.\nThe new Move glyph shows a part with three handles.\nPan keeps its four arrows.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo release gate, pixel snapshot run, Windows build, or wasm build.\nThe shell split, shell line-end conversion, and crate-wide formatting remain deferred by the recorded decision.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNo open PR changed a file in this patch at the overlap check.\nPRs #2256, #2149, and #1798 change `shell.rs`.\nPR #1798 has `needs-maintainer`.\nThis patch records the shell deferral and does not change that file.\nThis branch starts at upstream/main `8643d9bb7`.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: Release unused handle mesh caches and distinguish the Move glyph from Pan.\n\nFixes #2508\n\n",
